  "implementationFindings": [
    "The exact same strict fourteen source descriptors are selected; defaults, readonly state, format, cardinality, nativeType, option and target constraints remain enforced.",
    "Partition membership is exhaustive and disjoint by UTF8 source identity. A reused directory row must join the original resolved operation, prepared intent/spec/hash, original mapping and imported namespace; directory membership alone is insufficient.",
    "All-new uses the unchanged strict legacy supplement and closed v1 constructor. No partition field is emitted for v1, and injected fields are refused.",
    "Partial overlap constructs a missing-only plan bound to original source, namespace, checkpoint and partition. Every missing checkpoint intent and mapping is revalidated against that plan.",
    "All-present creates no second plan, executor call, supplemental journal/checkpoint or verification. Its explicit v2 reference binds the genuine original preservation checkpoint and the original definition directory.",
    "Current committed definition and namespace observations precede missing writes and follow completion, under the same account/run/lease and registered destination operation. Sequential observations are not a globally atomic schema snapshot.",
    "Cold v2 reconstruction recomputes exact partition and both source/provenance paths; equality of complete canonical reference bytes is required. Current definition reads expect original creation binding for reused rows and supplemental binding only for newly created rows.",
    "Cold all-present retains zero supplemental bindings. The caller must keep the v2 ordinary reference and pass the original shared journal parent to the still-required ordinaryPropertyJournalDirectory argument.",
    "Existing execute/produce path, ticket ownership, full source verification, E registered operation and final synchronous journal checks remain preserved by the reviewed source inverse; the actor hop still requires current App persistence ownership."
  ],
